# 🌙 Project LUNA — Interactive AI Vision Assistant

An AI-powered vision assistant that sees, understands, talks, and learns — with a stunning modern chat UI.

---

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph Frontend["Frontend (React + Vite + Tailwind)"]
        UI[Chat UI] --> Camera[Camera Preview]
        UI --> Input[Message Input]
        UI --> Results[Detection Results]
    end

    subgraph Backend["Backend (Flask API)"]
        API[Flask REST API]
        API --> OD[Object Detection - YOLO]
        API --> FR[Face Recognition]
        API --> ED[Emotion Detection]
        API --> SD[Sign Language Detection]
        API --> UH[Unknown Handler / Learning]
        API --> TR[Translator]
    end

    subgraph Storage["Storage Layer"]
        JSON1[learned_objects.json]
        JSON2[learned_faces.json]
        FACES[faces/ encodings]
    end

    Frontend -->|Axios HTTP| Backend
    Backend --> Storage
```

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Tailwind CSS**: You requested Tailwind CSS — I'll use **Tailwind CSS v3** with the Vite plugin. Please confirm if you want a different version.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Camera Access**: The camera preview will use the browser's `getUserMedia` API. Frames will be captured from a `<video>` element and sent to the backend as base64 images via the `/process` endpoint. This requires HTTPS in production (localhost works for development).

> [!WARNING]
> **Heavy AI Dependencies**: Libraries like `ultralytics` (YOLO), `face_recognition` (requires `dlib` + CMake), and `mediapipe` can be large and may require build tools. I'll provide clear setup instructions. Some models will use **placeholder logic** that's structured to support real models.

> [!NOTE]
> **Emotion Detection**: Instead of requiring a large custom model, I'll use a lightweight approach with `deepface` or a placeholder CNN. The architecture will support swapping in any real model.

