### Component 1: Backend — Flask API Server

#### [NEW] [app.py](file:///c:/Users/sk600/Documents/Project%20LUNA/backend/app.py)
- Flask application with CORS support
- **Endpoints:**
  - `POST /api/process` — Accepts base64 image, runs all detectors, returns JSON results
  - `POST /api/learn` — Accepts user label for unknown face/object, stores it
  - `GET /api/status` — Health check
  - `GET /api/history` — Get learned items
- Returns structured JSON:
```json
{
  "objects": [{"label": "bottle", "confidence": 0.92, "bbox": [...]}],
  "faces": [{"name": "Suneel", "location": [...]}],
  "emotion": "happy",
  "signs": ["hello"],
  "unknown_faces": [{"id": "face_001", "encoding": "..."}],
  "unknown_objects": [{"id": "obj_001", "crop": "base64..."}],
  "message": "I see Suneel looking happy! There's a bottle on the table.",
  "translations": {
    "en": "...",
    "ta": "...",
    "hi": "..."
  }
}
```

#### [NEW] [config.py](file:///c:/Users/sk600/Documents/Project%20LUNA/backend/config.py)
- Configuration for model paths, storage paths, confidence thresholds
- Debug/Production toggle

---

### Component 2: AI Detection Modules

#### [NEW] [object_detection.py](file:///c:/Users/sk600/Documents/Project%20LUNA/backend/models/object_detection.py)
- Uses `ultralytics` YOLO (YOLOv8n — nano model for speed)
- `detect_objects(frame)` → returns list of detected objects with labels, confidence, bounding boxes
- Falls back to placeholder if YOLO model not available
- Checks `learned_objects.json` for custom labels

#### [NEW] [face_recognition_module.py](file:///c:/Users/sk600/Documents/Project%20LUNA/backend/models/face_recognition_module.py)
- Uses `face_recognition` library for encoding & matching
- `detect_faces(frame)` → returns list of faces with names or "unknown"
- `learn_face(encoding, name)` → stores new face encoding
- Loads known faces from `storage/faces/` on startup

#### [NEW] [emotion_detection.py](file:///c:/Users/sk600/Documents/Project%20LUNA/backend/models/emotion_detection.py)
- Uses `deepface` library or a lightweight FER model
- `detect_emotion(frame, face_location)` → returns emotion label (happy, sad, angry, neutral, surprise, fear, disgust)
- Falls back to placeholder random detection if model unavailable

#### [NEW] [sign_detection.py](file:///c:/Users/sk600/Documents/Project%20LUNA/backend/models/sign_detection.py)
- Uses `mediapipe` for hand landmark detection
- Implements rule-based sign classification for: Hello, Yes, No, Thank You, Help, I Love You
- `detect_signs(frame)` → returns list of detected signs
- Landmark geometry analysis (finger positions, angles)

---

### Component 3: Learning System

#### [NEW] [unknown_handler.py](file:///c:/Users/sk600/Documents/Project%20LUNA/backend/learning/unknown_handler.py)
- `flag_unknown_face(encoding, face_id)` → stores temporarily, triggers chat question
- `flag_unknown_object(crop_image, obj_id)` → stores temporarily, triggers learning flow
- `learn_from_user(item_type, item_id, label)` → permanently stores the label
- Manages `learned_objects.json` and `learned_faces.json`

---

### Component 4: Utilities

#### [NEW] [translator.py](file:///c:/Users/sk600/Documents/Project%20LUNA/backend/utils/translator.py)
- Translates detection results to English, Tamil, and Hindi
- Uses `googletrans` or simple dictionary-based translation for common terms
- Falls back to English if translation fails

#### [NEW] [response_generator.py](file:///c:/Users/sk600/Documents/Project%20LUNA/backend/utils/response_generator.py)
- Generates natural, human-like response sentences from detection data
- Templates for different scenarios (known face, unknown face, emotions, objects, signs)
- Contextual awareness (combines multiple detections into one coherent message)

